{title: Blest Be the Tie That Binds}
{artist: John Fawcett}
{key: F}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 76}

Verse 1
[F]Blest be the [Bb]tie that [F]binds our [Bb]hearts in [C]Christian [F]love:
the fellowship of [Bb]kindred [F]minds is [Bb]like to [C]that a[F]bove.

Verse 2
Before our Father's throne
We pour our ardent prayers;
Our fears, our hopes,
our aims are one Our comforts and our cares.

Verse 3
We share each other's woes,
Our mutual burdens bear;
And often for each other flows The sympathizing tear.

Verse 4
When we asunder part,
It gives us inward pain;
But we shall still
be joined in heart, And hope to meet again.

Verse 5
This glorious hope revives
Our courage by the way;
While each in expectation lives, And longs to see the day.
